WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.030
<i>Imperial Nelpha.</i>

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.870
<i>A large, historic land, located to the west of the Roland Empire.</i>

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.380
<i>It used to war frequently with Roland,</i>

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.860
<i>but the current Nelphan Emperor, Gread, has worked towards domestic enrichment,</i>

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.300
<i>and has built a solid reputation as a good king.</i>

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.830
<i>Within the land are many ruins from prior ages.</i>

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.300
There are too many; I can't do this.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.290
Ah, I'm so tired... sleepy... hungry...

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.620
I can't see any dumpling shops.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.050
Hey, you. Go buy me some dumplings.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.450
Why me?

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.370
Because the stock I brought is starting to diminish.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.700
That's not an answer.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.290
Besides, I've had it. I've had my fill of investigating ruins and dumplings.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.820
Let's get some rest in one of these inns.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.070
An inn? I see. So that's your <i>modus operandi</i>.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:53.940
Huh?

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.970
I've read all about it!

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.080
A man invites a woman to an inn. Then it goes...

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:03.500
"I'll <i>never</i> do a thing, okay? I'm just a little tired, so I'm getting some sleep."

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.150
"Really? You really won't do anything?"

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.890
Then, when they reach the inn, the man becomes a wild beast, and says...

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.100
"Mwahaha! Time to eat!"

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.800
He runs rampant and wild!

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.620
You... I think you've got something wrong here.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.820
Indeed. A master degenerate like you, who attacks women both young and old,

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.890
would never take such a roundabout approach.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.030
Who are you calling a master degenerate?!

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:30.900
Now then, playtime is over. We're visiting the Royal Nelphan Library, aren't we?

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.470
That was... play? Just now?

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:38.930
I was played with.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.450
It should be full of good material about the heroes' relics.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.560
Quite. Finish your search quickly, then.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.830
Now, hold on! Can't you offer words more encouraging than those?

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.470
I mean, even if visual appeal is all you've got—

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:31.430
Uh, uhm... Haha, I suddenly feel <i>incredibly</i> motivated!

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.650
She's going to kill me one day, for sure.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.360
Wait!

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.570
Hey, you barbarians!

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:44.970
Barbarians?

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.200
That's right!

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.940
There will be no admittance of entry for barbaric, dangerous people

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:51.880
into this sacred font of knowledge!

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:55.740
Well, I suppose she doesn't exactly dress like the library type.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.710
Well, I suppose if a sex fiend were armed, they would be an extreme danger.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:04.300
I think your outfit is posing more of a problem here.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.390
A beauty may wear whatever she likes without posing problems.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.630
I'm kidding.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.640
You pass! You pass!

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:18.940
Surely, there can be no problems with beauties. Come, come inside!

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.000
Wait a minute! Why is it okay for her to enter?

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.760
You little brat!

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.170
What are you doing?

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.920
That little brat was the one who ran into me!

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.970
Now my suit's all dirty!

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.140
We want some compensation! Compensation!

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:35.260
Let go!
We want some compensation! Compensation!

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:36.130
Let go!

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.630
Let go of brother Toale!

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.230
Ibel, Telura, run!

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.810
You nuisances, get out of the way!

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.520
Thank...

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.560
Phew, that was close.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.800
Ah, that right there. That thing you're holding.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.800
That's the book I wanted to look up.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.390
That was a close call.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.020
What's your problem, you bastard?!

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.530
Say, could you—

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.160
That was dangerous, little girl.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.370
This man is a habitual criminal, an abductor of young girls.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.600
You little...

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.330
Wh-Who are you people?

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.030
L-Lord Toale!

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:33.050
Wow, this is amazing.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:36.100
Toale, get me all the books on that shelf.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.030
Understood.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.910
Now then, let's get this done...

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.380
That hurt, Ferris!

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:49.480
Hey, you! What nerve, ordering him around so casually! Don't get uppity!

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.360
Lord Toale is the grandson

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:56.170
of Lord Gread Nelphi, Emperor of Imperial Nelpha himself!

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:59.150
Oh, Toale. Get that black one up there, too.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.250
This one?

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.470
Yeah, that's the one. That should be everything.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:04.290
Are you even listening to me?!

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:06.820
Please just leave it at that, Uncle Gainel.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:11.330
B-But, if you let random nobodies order you around like this,

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.130
it will bring shame to the name of Imperial Nelpha!

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:17.770
Not showing proper gratitude to a rescuer would shame the Nelphan name far more.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:22.240
Besides, I was born from my father's dalliances here and there.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.720
I'm an abandoned child;

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.900
I'm not someone who needs to be elevated.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.900
Because my mother was of lowborn descent,

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:31.810
my siblings and I were confined to a single estate.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.450
That's the kind of people we are.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:37.700
B-But, sir, everyone in the land who considers Nelpha's future

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:42.560
finds you far more suited than Lord Starnel to...

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.490
Speak no further, Gainel.

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:48.000
To begin with, I am no such vessel.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.620
Ryner, are there any other books you need?

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:53.810
Sure. Just get that shelf over there.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:54.840
Got it.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.780
Hey, this book up here!

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.780
All right, come on.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:00.340
Up you go.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:05.650
I see what you mean. He does seem a little like Sion.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.120
It's such a shame.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.950
Lord Toale and his siblings are all abandoned,

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.560
without even proper parents...

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.030
I'm not so sure about that.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:15.480
<i>Okay, what we're looking for begins here...</i>

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:18.210
At the very least, to those kids...

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:20.160
What do you know?!

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:24.920
What do <i>you</i> know?

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:30.020
That should do it for the Saeles River flood control works plan.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.420
The problem is Lord Beryl's territorial development...

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.840
Lord Astal!

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.470
What's wrong, Fiole?

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.290
Don't "what's wrong" me!

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.870
How many hours will you continue working?

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:41.930
You still haven't touched your meal at all!

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:46.300
Sorry, sorry. By the way, how is the issue with Lord Kriade's tax payments coming along?

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:49.160
I've already written up a report on it.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.240
However, I will certainly not show it to you until you eat this meal!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:58.380
You're quite good, Fiole. I knew I was right to call you here.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.580
That's because this is the best way for me to repay you.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:08.440
If I hadn't met Your Majesty then, my sister and I would both be...

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:13.710
I sometimes wonder if someone of my low status deserves such happiness...

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:15.070
That's where you're wrong.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.230
It has nothing to do with status.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:20.600
Everyone should have happiness, no matter who they are.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:26.020
Of course, such a world can never naturally come to pass.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:30.400
But, what's most important is to never give up.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.360
To never give up...?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.690
Just because your status is low... Don't give up so easily.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:42.550
No matter who looks down upon you, you're never alone.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:44.450
You are certain to have many allies.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:50.380
I am truly glad that you have become the king of this land.

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.140
Wh-What's this, all of a sudden?

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.240
Come, now. Please, eat your meal and have a nap.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.330
After all, there's a ball tonight!

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:04.640
All right. But Fiole, take the weekend off.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.640
But, I'm...

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.160
For your sister. Go see her.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.070
Thank you very much.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:23.510
What's with the brooding face?

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:24.150
Claugh.

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:27.650
Mingling with the nobility is one of the King's biggest jobs, isn't it?

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.710
You just want to go yourself.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:36.520
Claugh certainly is a handful, with his irrepressible love of women.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:41.020
Calne. Why don't you go pay that so-called Mrs. Pearl a visit?

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:41.660
What?!

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:44.590
All right, I got it. Go wherever you'd like.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:45.470
My lord!

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.880
Those two, I swear...

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:52.490
They could stand to learn a bit from Fiole.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:56.550
Your Highness! Please, don't stay in such a little cranny.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:59.060
Come out towards the center!

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:03.380
Lord Beryl, and Lord Pearl. I hope you are enjoying yourselves?

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:08.290
I am dazzled, as always, by the splendor of the parties Your Majesty holds.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.380
This must be yet another of our young king's natural talents.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:16.730
Not at all. My seat on the throne is due to all of your strengths.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:24.870
<i>Count Klausberr, and Duke Stearied.</i>

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:28.970
<i>Those at the heart of the anti-royalist faction send their henchmen at me,</i>

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.810
<i>and refuse to come out themselves.</i>

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:35.310
Sion.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.340
Claugh. What is it?

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:41.240
A report just came in from a guardsman.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:45.160
Fiole's been... murdered.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.330
Fiole?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:53.610
Oh, yes. Wasn't he the commoner Your Majesty recently appointed as secretary?

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.980
A murder, of all things!

00:10:55.980 --> 00:11:00.070
Well, on the bright side, at least the one killed was a commoner.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:07.680
Quite right. After all, if a noble were to be killed, it would be a major problem!

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.240
Sion...

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:23.610
I suppose so. It truly is a relief that the one killed was a commoner.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.100
<i>Scum.</i>

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.620
It's my fault. It's all my fault!

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:57.600
Again, because my power wasn't strong enough!

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:59.240
Stop it, Sion.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.460
I understand. I won't do it again.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.810
<i>Eslina,</i>

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:20.550
<i>Sorry for taking so long to reply.</i>

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:24.300
<i>But your brother is relieved to hear that you are doing so well.</i>

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:28.690
<i>When I receive letters from you, I always feel inspired to do better.</i>

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:31.770
<i>Besides, I'm blessed with the master that I have.</i>

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:35.400
<i>Lord Astal, the King, is incredible.</i>

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:39.080
<i>He deals with commoners like me on equal terms.</i>

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:41.840
<i>He truly puts this kingdom first in his heart.</i>

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:45.950
Claugh. Take care of the funeral and burial arrangements.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:50.890
Calne, see to Eslina's safety... before the nobles reach her.

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:51.810
My lord.

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:06.810
What a fool you are.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.040
Don't praise me so highly.

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:14.650
Not when I have so little power...

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.880
Not when I cannot protect anything...

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:22.200
Fiole...

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:38.640
Sorrow.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:45.150
Hatred. Anger. Regret. Vengeance. Despair.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:49.280
If you desire retribution, I'll assist you.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:52.560
Shall we slaughter them all? I'm quite good at that, you know.

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:55.000
No, not yet.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.410
Now is not the time.

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.670
Can you endure until then?

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:00.950
I'll endure.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:04.720
Besides, if I choose retribution now...

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:08.440
Won't you kill me?

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:12.390
After all, there's no need for an incompetent king,

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:15.290
a king who doesn't grasp the times, or a king with a weak heart.

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:24.140
Truly... The two of you, on your carefree journey...

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:25.680
It makes me a little jealous.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:31.450
Give it back!

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.560
No way!

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:34.580
Come on, now, no fighting!

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:36.790
Hey, don't run!

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:38.150
Sorry about this, Toale.

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:40.080
Crashing at your place like this, I mean.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.820
Oh, it's fine. You can see how we are here.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.590
One or two more people isn't a big deal.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.380
Hm? What's this pie?

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.150
The lady at the general store brought it.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:54.660
She said to do your best, and to not lose against that fool of a crown prince.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:58.540
You get it rough too, don't you?

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:01.820
Everyone seems to have their own views,

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:04.770
but we're doing fine just the way we are.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:13.540
Between Sion and Toale, it's tough all over for royalty...

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.680
You wild beast! Prepare yourself!

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.650
Hey, y— Wait!

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.810
I'll protect my sister!

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.340
What are you doing?

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.680
Sister!

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:28.210
Iris?

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.240
Sister, Iris came to save you!

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.920
You went missing all of a sudden, it had me so worried!

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:36.230
I see. I apologize for that.

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:39.160
Sister? So, this is Ferris's little sister?

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:41.440
Yup. Isn't she beautiful, like me?

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.460
Oh, oh, and brother Sion,

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.680
he said that you'd been taken by a wicked wild beast,

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:48.260
and that you were on a journey to find the greatest dumplings of all!

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:52.890
So Iris, uhm, became brother Sion's special person in charge of carrying information!

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.130
So, basically, this girl is our liaison with Sion?

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.540
Iris is great, right? Right?

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.480
Quite. But you're missing something.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:02.930
I know!

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:05.940
Here. A Wynnit dumpling combination set!

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.060
100 points.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:09.010
Hooray!

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:11.990
Iris scored 100 points! Isn't that amazing? Isn't it?

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.340
Ah, sure. That's amazing, huh?

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:18.790
Oh no! If a child talks to a wild beast, they'll be ruined!

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:22.420
That's right. I'm sorry, Iris.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.530
I... I held a conversation with this wild beast...

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.860
No!

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.070
This is unforgiveable!

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:34.320
This is for my sister!

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.640
A visit to Imperial Nelpha?

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:53.290
As such, in order to make known the disposition of the new King of Roland,

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:57.200
and to show that Roland desires peace,

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:02.300
it may be wise to first pay a visit to historic Imperial Nelpha.

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:05.930
There is a growing number of internal matters which must be swiftly dealt with.

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:07.960
I cannot give you a decision as of now.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:11.950
Yes, my lord. I will be satisfied if you can simply keep it in mind,

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:15.240
and give it further consideration.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:16.410
It's a trap.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:20.110
If you went out on carefree trips, you'd be killed without a doubt.

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:21.660
Perhaps there are some in Nelpha

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:24.650
connected with the nobles of the anti-royalist faction?

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.290
It's highly possible.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:29.900
After all, even those in the anti-royalist faction

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.910
can't lay a hand on you inside Roland.

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:34.250
Instead, they got Fiole...

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.150
I beg your pardon.

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:45.090
There was no one here, so I took the liberty of waiting inside.

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:46.500
Who are you?

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.430
I am Miran Froaude.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.510
As the son of Marquis Karlal Froaude,

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:57.260
I currently hold the position of lieutenant colonel in the Imperial Roland Army.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.180
What does a noble's son want with the king?

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.240
I would ask about His Majesty the King's

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:07.130
secret gathering of talent with which to oppose the nobility.

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:08.520
You son of a—

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:09.110
Wait.

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:12.780
I know of you, Miran Froaude.

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:14.910
You became a second lieutenant at the young age of 17.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.950
Your outstanding talent had you promoted to lieutenant colonel in the blink of an eye.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:21.160
You are Marquis Foraude's son, but...

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.830
You were originally an orphan purchased by House Froaude.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:28.330
Furthermore, did the late Fiole Folkal not report

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.840
that I would resort to the foulest of measures to achieve a mission,

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:36.050
and that I would do anything for a promotion?

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:40.720
And what does one such as yourself want with me?

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:41.900
Well...

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:46.230
Claugh. Step out for a moment.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:47.490
Sion!

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.240
I wish to speak with him.

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:53.400
You just have to hear things out, don't you?

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.320
Sorry.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:55.900
Watch yourself.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:02.280
Well? What do you want with me?

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:06.330
You're the one who wants something, aren't you, Lord Sion Astal?

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.350
What?

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:12.610
It is because <i>you</i> need <i>me</i> that I came here.

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:15.490
Lights are gathering around you.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.080
Radiant, shining lights of hope.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:22.150
They offer the strength with which one can change this country.

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:26.390
However, that alone is not enough

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:28.310
to get that which you truly desire, is it not?

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:33.350
Will you continue bearing the darkness by yourself?

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:37.230
You cannot. You are the king of this land.

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:41.450
You must be everyone's light of hope. In which case...

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.470
Allow me to take your place, and bear the darkness.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:48.700
So that you may gain that which you truly seek.

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:54.710
You would claim to know what I seek?

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:59.830
Of course, I am aware of it.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:03.140
Oh? Then say it.

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:07.210
Right now, the Roland Empire remains little more

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:10.230
than a single kingdom on the continent of Menoris.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:15.300
However, you can raise the flag you bear over the entire continent,

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:18.540
the flag of the Grand Roland Empire.

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:28.310
That's quite an outrageous dream!

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:32.520
I hate to disappoint you, but all I desire is a kingdom with no war,

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:34.920
where the people can live happily.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:36.650
But of course.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:41.380
Regardless of what may dwell in his heart, a king must proclaim such intents.

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:44.810
I shall bear the darkness that remains.

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:50.020
For that purpose, I would even be willing to dispose of my own father personally.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:54.510
Please, place me at your side.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:07.300
You don't wish to kill your father, do you?

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:09.960
That's quite the jest.

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:35.290
Very well. You shall work for me.

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:40.330
You have my deepest gratitude.

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:24.130
<i>Guard duty really sucks.</i>

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:27.300
<i>Well, if a king is that atrocious,</i>

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:29.670
<i>I guess he'd be targeted by tons of enemies.</i>

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:31.960
<i>So do something about it yourself, jeez!</i>

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:34.830
<i>Don't rely on me! What a pain.</i>
